# Contributing Guidelines

We love contributions from everyone! By participating in this project, you agree to abide by its [code of conduct](link/to/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).

Here are some guidelines to help you get started:

## Ways to Contribute

*   **Report Bugs:** Use the [issue tracker](link/to/issue/tracker) to report bugs. Please include steps to reproduce the issue and relevant system information.
*   **Suggest Enhancements:** We welcome ideas for new features. Please use the [issue tracker](link/to/issue/tracker) to propose enhancements and explain why they would be valuable to the project.
*   **Code Contributions:**
    *   Fork the repository and create a new branch for your changes.
    *   Ensure your code follows the project's [style guide](link/to/STYLE_GUIDE.md) (if you have one).
    *   Add tests for your code to ensure it works correctly and doesn't break existing functionality.
    *   Write clear, concise [commit messages](link/to/commit/guide).
    *   Submit a pull request (PR) to the `main` branch. Provide a clear description of your changes and reference the issue it addresses.

## Development Process

*   **Code Review:** All pull requests will be reviewed by maintainers. We may provide constructive feedback or ask for changes.
*   **Commit Signing:** You may be required to sign a Contributor License Agreement (CLA) or certify your contributions.

## Resources for New Contributors

If you're new to contributing to open source, check out the [Open Source Guides](https://opensource.guide/how-to-contribute/) for helpful information on the process.

Thank you for helping make this project better!